// Oxikube keymap: your key bindings, layered on top of the built-in defaults.
// Saving this file applies it at once. A binding that cannot be used (an unknown action, a
// keystroke that does not parse) is skipped and listed in a notification with its line
// (keymap.json:<line>); every other binding still applies.
//
// Each section has an optional "context" (where the binding is active), an optional
// "use_key_equivalents" (keep shortcuts working on non-US keyboard layouts) and "bindings".
// A binding maps a keystroke (or a sequence such as "ctrl-k ctrl-s") to an action name, to
// ["action name", { ...data }], or to null to unbind a default key. Later sections and later
// bindings win. The command palette lists every action name.
//
// [
//   {
//     "context": "ResourceTable && !Editing",
//     "bindings": {
//       "y": "resource_table::ViewDescribe",   // y now opens Describe instead of YAML
//       "ctrl-d": null                          // free the key
//     }
//   }
// ]
[]
